  "title": "House of Wisdom (Bayt al-Hikma), Baghdad",
  "summary": "The Bayt al-Hikma, or House of Wisdom, was a library and translation centre in Abbasid Baghdad. Some reports say Caliph al-Ma’mun founded it in the early 830s; some historians see it as an extension of a library that already existed under Harun al-Rashid. Under al-Ma’mun, Persian and Greek works were translated into Arabic.",
